I have everything needed. Here is the complete picture of the current implementation.

## Important upfront finding: spec/implementation mismatch

The acceptance test comments describe an **"identity-key-v2"** design that is **NOT implemented**. The test at `AcceptanceTest.java` claims `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))` producing a 64-hex string, and that duplicate detection (409) keys off it. The **actual code does none of this**: `IdentityKey.of` returns a plain pipe-joined string `telephone|email|householdId` (not hashed, not 64-hex), there is **no soundex anywhere** (no `Soundex` class, no `commons-codec` in `pom.xml` — only the test comment mentions it), and duplicate detection keys off a `householdId` derived from `(lastName, postcode)`, not telephone/email/soundex. So `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserts a 64-hex shape that the current `IdentityKey.of` cannot satisfy.

## 1. Files involved in owner creation & duplicate detection

Endpoint wiring:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — the full create pipeline

Owner functions (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`):
- `EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` — the hard 409 duplicate block
- `Households.java` — householdId / member-count / max-level helper
- `AssignHousehold.java` — stamps householdId on new owner
- `AssignHouseholdSize.java` — records household size
- `AssignPossibleDuplicate.java` — the soft-match flag
- `RejectDisposableEmail.java` + `DisposableEmailDomains.java` — email-domain blocklist (400)
- `NormalizeOwnerEmail.java` + `EmailNormalizer.java` — lower-cased email + `domainOf`
- `NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java` + `TelephoneNormalizer.java` — E.164 normalized telephone
- `AssignCustomerCode.java` — customer code
- `ValidateOwnerFields.java`, `BuildOwner.java`, `SaveOwner.java`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`, plus idempotency/registration/city/daily-limit steps

Util:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/IdentityKey.java` — the response-surfaced identity key
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Sha256.java` — shared SHA-256 hex
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CustomerCode.java`

Model / mapper:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — fields `householdId`, `householdSize`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `customerCode`, `deleted`, etc.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — maps `identityKey` onto the response via `IdentityKey.of(owner)`

Escalation (409):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml`

## 2. Exact current computations

**identityKey** (`IdentityKey.java`) — pipe-joined, NOT hashed:
```java
public static String of(Owner owner) {
    return of(owner.getTelephone(), owner.getEmail(), owner.getHouseholdId());
}
public static String of(String telephone, String email, String householdId) {
    return orEmpty(telephone) + '|' + orEmpty(email) + '|' + orEmpty(householdId);
}
private static String orEmpty(String value) {
    return (value == null || value.isBlank()) ? "" : value;
}
```

**householdId** (`Households.householdId`) — first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`; null when postcode blank:
```java
static String householdId(String lastName, String postcode) {
    if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) {
        return null;
    }
    return Sha256.hex(normalizeName(lastName) + '|' + postcode).substring(0, 12);
}
private static String normalizeName(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.strip().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```
`Sha256.hex` = lower-case hex SHA-256 of UTF-8 bytes. `AssignHousehold` stamps it: `owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()))`.

**soundex** — does not exist anywhere in the codebase (only named in a test comment).

**normalizedTelephone** (`TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`) — strips `[\s()-]`, keeps country code if `+`-prefixed else assumes AU `+61` dropping one leading `0`; requires `[0-9]{8,15}` and a country-specific national length (`+61`→9, `+1`→10). `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (400) on null result and stores the E.164 value in the `OwnerFieldsDto`.

**lowerEmail** (`EmailNormalizer`): `normalize` = `email.trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT)`; validity via regex `^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9-]+(\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$`; `domainOf` = lower-cased substring after last `@`. `NormalizeOwnerEmail` leaves null/blank untouched, else validates (throws `InvalidEmailException` 400) and stores lower-cased.

**email-domain blocklist** (`DisposableEmailDomains`):
```java
private static final Set<String> BLOCKED = Set.of(
        "mailinator.com", "tempmail.com", "guerrillamail.com");
static boolean isDisposable(String email) {
    String domain = EmailNormalizer.domainOf(email);
    return domain != null && BLOCKED.contains(domain);
}
```
`RejectDisposableEmail` throws `DisposableEmailException` → **400** (`BAD_REQUEST`) for a blocked domain.

**soft-match logic** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`): skips flagging when `sharesHousehold=true`; otherwise iterates non-deleted owners and flags on same postcode (non-blank, exact equals) AND same last name (case-folded via `strip().toLowerCase`) AND **different** telephone:
```java
private static boolean isPossibleDuplicate(Owner candidate, Owner existing) {
    return samePostcode(candidate.getPostcode(), existing.getPostcode())
        && sameLastName(candidate.getLastName(), existing.getLastName())
        && !Objects.equals(candidate.getTelephone(), existing.getTelephone());
}
```
First match wins; sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=existing.getId()`, else false/null.

## 3. Where the 409 is generated

`EnsureUniqueIdentity.service` (hard block, runs before build under `govern: [ transaction ]`): returns early if `sharesHousehold=true` or `householdId==null`; otherwise scans non-deleted owners and throws `DuplicateIdentityException(householdId)` when an existing owner has the **same householdId AND same telephone**:
```java
if (householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())
        && Objects.equals(request.getTelephone(), existing.getTelephone())) {
    throw new DuplicateIdentityException(householdId);
}
```
`DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.handle` maps it to `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CONFLICT).body(new Error(ex.getMessage()))` — body `{"error": "Household already registered: <householdId>"}`. Wired via the escalation YAML `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml`.

Note the current 409 rule is "same household **and same telephone**" (i.e. same person re-registering). A same-household **different-telephone** request is allowed through and merely soft-flagged.

